# Stoqly Project Rules

These rules take precedence over swiftui.mdc and inventory.mdc for this project.

## 1. SwiftData Save — ALWAYS use safeSave

```swift
// ✅ ALWAYS
modelContext.safeSave(context: "DescriptiveContextLabel")

// ❌ NEVER — swallows errors silently
try? modelContext.save()
try! modelContext.save()
```

`safeSave` is in `Utilities/ModelContextExtension.swift`. The `context:` string appears in logs. No exceptions.

## 2. ActivityEvent BEFORE Delete

When deleting any item, capture the activity event BEFORE calling delete — the `storage` relationship is nil after delete.

```swift
// ✅ CORRECT
let event = ActivityEvent(eventType: "ItemDeleted", itemName: item.name, storageName: item.storage?.name ?? "Unknown")
modelContext.insert(event)
modelContext.delete(item)
modelContext.safeSave(context: "DeleteItem")

// ❌ WRONG — storageName will be empty/nil
modelContext.delete(item)
let event = ActivityEvent(...)
```

## 3. Barcode Scanner — fullScreenCover ONLY

```swift
// ✅ CORRECT
.fullScreenCover(isPresented: $showScanner) { BarcodeScannerView(...) }

// ❌ WRONG — AVFoundation XPC pipeline breaks in sheets (err=-17281)
.sheet(isPresented: $showScanner) { BarcodeScannerView(...) }
```

## 4. Quantity vs Currency Display

```swift
// ✅ Quantities — use smartFormatted
Text(item.currentQuantity.smartFormatted)   // "5", "2.5", "0"

// ✅ Monetary values — use currencyManager.formatPrice()
Text(currencyManager.formatPrice(item.unitCost))  // "₹400.00"

// ❌ NEVER hardcode a currency symbol
Text("$\(item.unitCost)")
Text(String(format: "%.2f", item.unitCost))  // missing symbol
```

`smartFormatted` is a `Double` extension in `ModelContextExtension.swift`.

## 5. Currency — Never Hardcode the Symbol

All monetary values must go through `currencyManager.formatPrice(amount)`.
Never write `"$"`, `"₹"`, `"€"` as string literals in Views.
`CurrencyManager` is provided as `.environmentObject()` from the root — use `@EnvironmentObject var currencyManager: CurrencyManager` in any view that shows prices.
Never create a new `@StateObject private var currencyManager = CurrencyManager()` inside a child view — there is ONE instance at the root.

## 6. NavigationStack — Never Nest in Modal Views

`ItemDetailView` must NOT contain a `NavigationStack` in its body. Sheet callers provide one:

```swift
// ✅ Sheet caller wraps it
.sheet(isPresented: $show) {
    NavigationStack { ItemDetailView(item: item) }
}

// ❌ ItemDetailView must NOT have NavigationStack inside it
```

`AddStorageView` already has its own `NavigationStack` — never wrap it in another one.

## 7. Sheets — Always Use sheetStyle()

```swift
.sheet(isPresented: $show) {
    SomeView().sheetStyle()
}
```

`sheetStyle()` is in `Views/Components/SheetStyle.swift`.

## 8. isPro — NEVER Hardcode true

`SubscriptionManager.isPro` is currently `true` for testing. NEVER set it to `true` in any new code or spec. Never reference `isPro = true` in comments or code. Use the proper gate:

```swift
guard SubscriptionManager.shared.canAddItem(currentItemCount: storage.items.count) else {
    showingItemLimitPaywall = true
    return
}
```

## 9. ViewModel Pattern

```swift
@MainActor
final class SomeViewModel: ObservableObject {
    @Published private(set) var filteredItems: [InventoryItem] = []
    private var items: [InventoryItem] = []

    func bind(items: [InventoryItem]) {
        self.items = items
        applyFilters()
    }
}
```

- ViewModels are `@MainActor final class` conforming to `ObservableObject`
- Never inject `modelContext` into a ViewModel — Views handle all SwiftData operations
- Pass data/IDs to ViewModels, not model objects with active contexts

## 10. Navigation — No Coordinators

This project uses SwiftUI native navigation (NavigationLink, .sheet, .fullScreenCover). Do NOT introduce Coordinator classes or patterns — they are explicitly not used here.

## 11. SwiftData New Fields — Use Default Values

When adding a new field to an existing `@Model` class, always provide a default value so SwiftData handles migration automatically without a VersionedSchema:

```swift
// ✅ Safe lightweight migration
var sellingPrice: Double = 0
var reorderPercentage: Double = 0

// ❌ Requires explicit migration
var sellingPrice: Double  // no default
```

## 12. Alerts — Standard .alert is Fine

The `swiftui.mdc` rule banning `alert()` does NOT apply here. Standard `.alert` and `.confirmationDialog` are used throughout this codebase for delete confirmations and warnings. Do not replace them with custom views.

## 13. Custom Navigation Headers

Most views use a custom nav header instead of `.navigationTitle`. Do not replace custom headers with standard NavigationView titles — it changes the visual design.

## 14. Bundle ID and App Name

- Bundle ID: `com.vishuddhi.stoqly`
- App name in all Maestro flows and assertions: `"Stoqly"` (not "Smart Inventory")

## 15. New ActivityEvent Types for Phase 7A

When creating sale or movement events, use these exact eventType strings:
- `"SaleMade"` — when a SaleEvent is recorded
- `"MovementLogged"` — when an InventoryMovement (non-sale) is recorded

Insert the ActivityEvent BEFORE any modelContext.delete() call (rule 2 above).
